I[53]="MIXED, one headline — the BLUFF read. The sandbagging Regents lead with their weakest cards (Omarzaii, Norrtje, Maharaaj) and keep three aces (Buttler, Raahul, Najibullaah); in the fog the swipe follows a fixed, public rule: a LOUD (Aggressive) call is always a weak number — bottom 60% of the game for that stat — and a strong number is always called quietly. Aha: invert the read — beat a loud call with a mid card (it pays +2 and takes a wicket) and keep MacCalum and Mahmudullaah for the quiet calls; the bluff tracker counts how every loud call turned out, and your Review covers one quiet big loss."
